# ---- R session data & history (never commit these) ----
.RData
.Rhistory
.Rapp.history
.Rproj.user/
.Ruserdata/

# ---- macOS junk ----
.DS_Store

# ---- Manuscripts & office documents: NEVER publish to this public repo ----
*.docx
*.doc
*.pptx
~$*.docx

# ---- Editor / tool folders ----
.claude/

# ---- Data files (kept off GitHub; too large / not for public repo) ----
*.xlsx
*.csv
*.rds

# ---- Generated outputs (plots, reports) ----
*.png
*.pdf

# ---- Archived output figures ----
Archive/

# ---- Exploratory serology work, not part of the CHIKV/MAYV pipeline ----
# FOI.R fitted Rsero force-of-infection models to Abad-Franch_seroprevalence.xlsx. No
# current script sources either, so both are kept locally but off the public repo.
# NOTE: CHIKV_ca_lhs.R hardcodes the FOI prior as 0.008 (0.003-0.020), commented
# "from serology" -- FOI.R is the derivation, so keep a local copy for the record.
FOI.R
Abad-Franch_seroprevalence.xlsx

# ---- Excel/LibreOffice lock files ----
~$*

# ---- REPLICATION data: the sampled parameter values behind the published estimates ----
# Two stages per pathogen. Stage 1 = the transmission LHS (*_ca_lhs.R); stage 2 = the
# burden LHS drawn inside the engine. The CHIKV pair joins on `transmission_row`, since
# that engine resamples the stage-1 ensemble with replacement; for MAYV the pairing is 1:1.
# Scenario-tagged copies (e.g. MAYV_ca_burden_draws_high.csv) stay ignored.
# Leading "/" anchors these to the repo root ON PURPOSE: without it the negation matches
# the basename at any depth, which would un-ignore the stale archived copies sitting in
# Outputs_*/ and publish snapshots that no longer match the current model.
!/CHIKV_ca_lhs_draws.csv
!/CHIKV_ca_burden_draws.csv
!/MAYV_ca_lhs_draws.csv
!/MAYV_ca_burden_draws.csv

# ---- INPUT data: hand-maintained source parameters, MUST be tracked ----
# (the *.xlsx / *.csv rules above ignore generated outputs; these are exceptions)
!beta_hyolim.xlsx
!costs.xlsx
!disease_progression.xlsx
!model_calibration.xlsx
!mortality_2024.xlsx
!population.xlsx
!population_MAYV.xlsx
!weekly_case.xlsx
# NOTE: rainfall.xlsx (129 MB) exceeds GitHub's 100 MB file limit and stays ignored.
#       Source: see rainfall_season.R / extract_caldas_rainfall.R for provenance.
